{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.positive_b3_forces_above_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.positive_b3_forces_above_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L327-L337","doc":"**The escape requires a non-minimal Brunnian carrier.** Any `c₃` reaching a positive\n`b₃/b₂` at all needs `c₃ > 6` — strictly more than the Borromean's crossing number,\nwhich `QOU.Knots.KauffmanTL3` machine-checks is the *minimum* over nontrivial Brunnian\n3-braids. With parity (§3b) the next available value is `c₃ = 8`, not `7`.\n\n**The corpus's selection principle is NOT minimality** — see the header's §\"What has\nnever been searched\". It is Frobenius-residual minimisation; length is only a tiebreak. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.single_brunnian_carrier_integer_valued","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.single_brunnian_carrier_integer_valued","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L319-L325","doc":"**A single Brunnian `A = 3` carrier does worse still.** Then `μ_triple = c₃/2` with `c₃`\neven, so `b₃/b₂` is an *integer*: the nearest positive value is `1` at `c₃ = 8`, **55.98 %**\nhigh, and `0` at the Borromean `c₃ = 6` is the degenerate locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.even_lattice_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.even_lattice_gap","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L297-L317","doc":"**Under parity the grid coarsens to the half-integers, and the gap widens.** With\n`c(³H)` and `c(³He)` both even their sum is even, so `μ_triple = (c_H + c_He)/4` is a\n*half*-integer, not a quarter-integer: the lattice is `k/2 - 3`. Every point stays at\nleast `209293/1483044 ≈ 0.14112` from the measured ratio — **22.01 %** of it, up from the\n16.98 % that ignoring parity allows.\n\nThis is what excludes the two nearest points of `quarter_lattice_gap`: `c₃ = 7` and\n`c(³H)+c(³He) = 15` are both **odd**, hence unreachable by Brunnian carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.brunnian_crossings_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.brunnian_crossings_even","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L290-L295","doc":"**Brunnian ⇒ even.** `BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_signedChannel_zero` empties the\nsigned channel exactly when `n₊ = n₋`; then `c = n₊ + n₋ = 2n₊` is even. The `A = 2` Hopf\ncarrier is *not* Brunnian (`lk = 1`, `n₊ = 2`, `n₋ = 0`) — it is the boundary case where\n`lk = z = 1` — so this constrains the `A ≥ 3` carriers only, which is where `b₃` lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.quarter_lattice_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.quarter_lattice_gap","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L271-L286","doc":"**And it misses by a fixed amount.** Every quarter-integer lattice point stays at\nleast `161468/1483044 ≈ 0.10887` from the measured ratio — `16.98 %` of it. The nearest\nis `m = 15`, i.e. `c(³H) + c(³He) = 15`; the half-integer grid of a *single* `A = 3`\ncarrier is a sublattice, so it misses by at least as much (in fact `c₃ = 7`, `22.01 %`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.no_quarter_lattice_point_is_measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.no_quarter_lattice_point_is_measured","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L256-L269","doc":"**No integer carrier assignment reproduces the measured `b₃`.** With `c₂ = 2` and\n`μ_triple` the isospin average of two integer crossing counts, `b₃/b₂` lands on the\nquarter-integer lattice `m/4 - 3`, which misses `rMeasured` for every `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.rMeasured_mem_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.rMeasured_mem_gap","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L251-L254","doc":"The measured ratio sits strictly inside the gap `(1/2, 3/4)` of the\nquarter-integer lattice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.rMeasured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.rMeasured","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L247-L249","doc":"The measured `b₃/b₂` from AME2020, exactly:\n`b₂ = 2.224566`, `B̄(3) = 8.0999205`, `b₃ = B̄(3) - 3b₂ = 1.4262225`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.muOfCrossings_halving_immaterial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.muOfCrossings_halving_immaterial","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L238-L243","doc":"The `½` in particular is not load-bearing: reading `μ = c` rather than `μ = c/2`\ngives the identical ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_scale_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_scale_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L218-L236","doc":"**Rescaling the multiplicity changes nothing.** `b₃/b₂` is invariant under\n`μ ↦ κμ` for any `κ ≠ 0`, so every result below holds for *any* multiplicity\nproportional to the crossing count — the `½` of `countChannel` is not load-bearing.\n\nThis matters for how the obstruction can be escaped, and it corrects the obvious\nguess. The `½` looks like a free convention one could simply drop; it is not, and\ndropping it would not help anyway. It is the unique solution of\n`BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy_decomp`, the `ring` identity splitting\n`n₊q − n₋q⁻¹` into its bar-even and bar-odd parts — and by this lemma any other\nconstant gives the same `b₃/b₂`.\n\nSo the hypothesis actually in force is **linearity**: `μ = κ·c`. Escaping the\nlattice needs a *nonlinear* `μ(c)`, and that contradicts `pairEnergy_decomp`\nbeing linear in `(n₊, n₋)`, which it is by construction. The escape route\ntherefore runs through `def:crossing-energy` itself, not through a convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.straddle_manufactures_the_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.straddle_manufactures_the_sign","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L208-L213","doc":"🛑 **The straddle.** `c₂ = 2` from the owner-ruled Hopf deuteron against `c₃ = 7`\nfrom the census A = 3 row gives the right sign — from two different assignments. Not a\nresult; recorded so the coincidence is not rediscovered as one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.census_carrier_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.census_carrier_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L201-L206","doc":"Census volume-match read consistently (`c₂ = 6` from `6₂`, `c₃ = 7` from the average\nof `8₁₁` and `L6a4`): `-11/6`. Recorded for completeness — the tier is AME-inverted and\nis not a derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.borromean_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.borromean_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L195-L199","doc":"Canonical Brunnian carriers (Hopf, Borromean `L6a4`): `c₃ = 6`, exactly the\ndegenerate locus. Agrees with `CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_b3_eq_zero`,\nreached here from the crossing counts rather than from `n₊`/`n₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.chain_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.chain_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L191-L193","doc":"One clasp per interface (the chain, `z = A-1`): `c₃ = 4`, `b₃/b₂ = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.enumerated_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.enumerated_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L187-L189","doc":"Min-length enumeration: `σ_g²` for every nucleus, so `c₃ = 2` and `b₃/b₂ = -2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_hopf_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_hopf_pair","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L179-L183","doc":"**With the owner-ruled Hopf pair carrier (`c₂ = 2`) the whole thing is one\ninteger.** This is the step the earlier retraction was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_of_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio_of_crossings","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L171-L177","doc":"**`b₃/b₂` is a ratio of crossing counts.** The factor of `½` cancels, so the\nmultiplicity convention drops out and only `c₃/c₂` survives. No hypothesis on `c₂` is\nneeded: the cancellation is an identity of `Field` division, degenerate case included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.bRatio","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L167-L169","doc":"`b₃/b₂` as a function of the pair and triple multiplicities\n(`CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3_over_b2_eq` — the scale has already cancelled). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.muOfCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation.muOfCrossings","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CarrierCrossingQuantisation.lean#L163-L165","doc":"The count-channel multiplicity of a carrier with crossing count `c`, namely\n`(n₊ + n₋)/2 = c/2` (`QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.countChannel`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}